ot wear a fake moustache that causes laughter in church.","Alabama, USA"],["It is illegal to whistle underwater.","Vermont, USA"],["Bingo games may not last longer than five hours.","North Carolina, USA"],["Cars must be driven with someone walking in front waving a red flag.","Historic, Pennsylvania, USA"],["It is illegal to sell your children's eyes.","Texas, USA"],["You may not walk a camel down the main street.","Nevada, USA"],["Elephants must be kept on a leash when walking down the street.","Orlando, Florida, USA"],["It is illegal to fall asleep in a cheese factory.","South Dakota, USA"],["Pickles must bounce to be legally sold as pickles.","Connecticut, USA"],["It is illegal to hunt camels.","Arizona, USA"],["Chewing gum may not be imported or sold.","Singapore"],["You must name your baby from a government-approved list.","Denmark"],["It is illegal to die in the Houses of Parliament.","United Kingdom"],["Stepping on banknotes is forbidden because they bear the King's image.","Thailand"],["It is illegal to run out of fuel on the Autobahn.","Germany"],["Feeding pigeons in St Mark's Square is banned.","Venice, Italy"],["Wearing high heels at ancient monuments is forbidden.","Greece"],["Building a sandcastle on the beach can get you fined.","Eraclea, Italy"],["Owning just one guinea pig is illegal because they get lonely.","Switzerland"],["You may not flush the toilet after 10 p.m. in an apartment.","Switzerland"],["It is illegal to carry a plank of wood along a pavement.","London, United Kingdom"],["Handling a salmon in suspicious circumstances is an offence.","United Kingdom"],["It is illegal to be drunk in charge of a cow.","Scotland"],["Naming a pig Napoleon is forbidden.","France"],["Kissing on railway platforms was banned to avoid delaying trains.","France"],["Video games involving violence must not be sold in internet cafés.","Greece"],["Men must not wear a skirt in public unless it is a kilt.","Historic, various"],["It is illegal to frown at a pig.","Historic, cited online"],["You may not lie down on a sidewalk.","Marshalltown, Iowa, USA"],["Kisses may last no longer than five minutes.","Iowa, USA"],["It is illegal to wear a hat that obstructs people's view in a theatre.","Massachusetts, USA"],["Fishing for whales in landlocked waters is prohibited.","Ohio, USA"],["You may not get a fish drunk.","Ohio, USA"],["It is illegal to have a sweaty horse on the streets.","Historic, Oklahoma, USA"],["Mispronouncing the state's name is frowned on by law.","Arkansas, USA"],["It is illegal to sing off-key.","North Carolina, USA"],["Bathing more than once a day is prohibited.","Historic, Boston, USA"],["Ferrets may not be kept as pets.","California, USA"],["It is illegal to peel an orange in a hotel room.","California, USA"],["Animals may not mate within 1,500 feet of a tavern, school or church.","California, USA"],["It is illegal to sell a car on Sunday.","Illinois, USA"],["You must have a permit to wear a mask in public.","Historic, New York, USA"],["Lions may not be taken to the movies.","Baltimore, Maryland, USA"],["It is illegal to keep a horse in a bathtub.","Utah, USA"],["Carrying a violin in a paper bag is forbidden.","Utah, USA"],["Ice cream may not be eaten on Sundays.","Historic, Illinois, USA"],["Every house must have a lawn mower in working order.","Historic, cited online"],["You may not shoot open a can of food.","Historic, cited online"],["It is illegal to drive blindfolded.","Alabama, USA"],["You may not dye a duckling blue and offer it for sale unless you sell more than six.","Kentucky, USA"],["Children may not dye chickens, ducklings or rabbits.","Historic, Florida, USA"],["Dancing on a moving train is prohibited.","Historic, cited online"]],"twist":["Twist: every message must rhyme.","Twist: you must mention a pelican at least once per team.","Twist: argue as if you were a 1920s radio announcer.","Twist: no message may be longer than ten words.","Twist: one player per team must argue only in questions.","Twist: cite a completely made-up expert by name.","Twist: argue as if your grandmother's honour depends on it."],"alias":["Purple Otter","Silver Fox","Velvet Moose","Neon Heron","Quiet Walrus","Copper Lynx","Paper Tiger","Lunar Moth","Rusty Badger","Glass Owl","Mint Gecko","Saffron Crow","Cobalt Hare","Amber Newt","Ivory Wolf","Lemon Shark"],"tf_starter":["What's a weirdly specific thing you love?","Describe your last meal like it's a crime scene.","What would your villain origin story be?","Name a hill you'd die on.","What's your most useless talent?","If you were a kitchen appliance, which one and why?"],"tf_hint":["The saviour is trying a little too hard to be liked.","Watch who keeps agreeing with everyone.","Someone here is steering the conversation on purpose.","The quiet ones aren't always the innocent ones.","Flattery is a weapon tonight — follow it."],"deal_event":["A rival swoops in with a competing offer.","A news leak makes one side look desperate.","Head office wants this closed in the next 60 seconds.","A supply shortage changes what's on the table.","An unexpected ally publicly backs one side."],"deal":[{"title":"The Food Truck & the Secret Recipe","setup":"A famous taco truck wants to buy a retiring chef's legendary salsa recipe.","terms":["Price","Credit on the menu","Exclusivity","Chef cameo nights"],"A":{"name":"Taco Truck","brief":"You need this salsa to survive a brutal food-court war. Regulars are drifting away.","ideal":"Buy it outright, cheap, with full exclusivity.","walkaway":"Walk if it costs more than a month of profit.","leverage":"You're the only buyer who'll keep the chef's name alive."},"B":{"name":"Retiring Chef","brief":"This recipe is your legacy, but you quietly need cash for one last trip.","ideal":"A big payday and your name on every cup forever.","walkaway":"Walk if you get no credit at all.","leverage":"Two other trucks have been sniffing around."}},{"title":"The Band & the Festival Slot","setup":"An indie band negotiates with a festival for a better stage and set time.","terms":["Stage size","Set time","Pay","Travel covered"],"A":{"name":"The Band","brief":"This slot could break you nationally, but your drummer just quit and you're broke.","ideal":"Main stage, sunset slot, travel paid.","walkaway":"Walk if you're stuck at noon on the tiny stage.","leverage":"Your single is unexpectedly going viral this week."},"B":{"name":"Festival Org","brief":"You have a 4pm hole in the lineup and a tight budget after a rainy year.","ideal":"Fill the slot cheap, no travel costs.","walkaway":"Walk if they demand headliner pay.","leverage":"A hundred other bands want this slot."}},{"title":"The Landlord & the Llama","setup":"A tenant wants to keep a pet llama; the landlord wants it gone.","terms":["Pet deposit","Rent change","Llama outdoor hours","Lease length"],"A":{"name":"Tenant","brief":"The llama is emotionally essential and weirdly great for your socials.","ideal":"Keep the llama, no rent increase.","walkaway":"Walk (move out) if the llama has to go.","leverage":"You're the only tenant who pays on time, and the building is half empty."},"B":{"name":"Landlord","brief":"Other tenants are complaining, but vacancies are killing you.","ideal":"Llama gone, or a fat deposit and higher rent.","walkaway":"Walk if the llama does damage with no deposit.","leverage":"The lease technically bans 'livestock'."}},{"title":"The Startup Split","setup":"Two co-founders renegotiate equity as one steps back from day-to-day.","terms":["Equity kept","Title","Vesting","Future buy-back"],"A":{"name":"Staying Founder","brief":"You do all the work now and investors are nervous about a ghost founder.","ideal":"Claw back most of their equity, keep CEO.","walkaway":"Walk (threaten to quit) if they keep control.","leverage":"You hold every key customer relationship."},"B":{"name":"Leaving Founder","brief":"You built the core product and need the upside, but you're exhausted.","ideal":"Keep your equity and an advisor title, no clawback.","walkaway":"Walk if pushed below a fair share for what you built.","leverage":"You own the original codebase and the brand name."}},{"title":"The Double-Booked Garden","setup":"Two couples accidentally booked the same wedding garden for the same Saturday.","terms":["Who gets the date","Cost split","Time of day","The good gazebo"],"A":{"name":"Couple Rosewood","brief":"Your family flew in from overseas; moving the date is a disaster.","ideal":"Keep the date and the gazebo, split costs evenly.","walkaway":"Walk if you lose the date entirely.","leverage":"You booked 20 minutes earlier and have the email."},"B":{"name":"Couple Marigold","brief":"Your deposit is non-refundable and your caterer is locked in.","ideal":"Keep the date and gazebo, pay less.","walkaway":"Walk if forced to move to Sunday.","leverage":"The venue owner is your cousin."}}]}$c$::jsonb) k, jsonb_array_elements(k.value) with ordinality e(value, ord)
